hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1199","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Duraqi and Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, saying: Hushaym told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aisha about the voluntary prayers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “He used to pray four times before noon in My house, then he would go out and lead the people in prayer, then he would return to my house and pray two rak’ahs, and he used to lead the people in Maghrib prayer, then he would return to my house. He would pray two rak'ahs, then he would lead the evening prayer with them, then he would enter my house and pray two rak'ahs, and he used to pray nine rak'ahs at night, including the Witr prayer. And when dawn came, he would pray two rak’ahs, then he would go out and lead the people in the dawn prayer.”"
